<title>USA: U.S. weekend box office chart -- May 16-18.</title>
<headline>U.S. weekend box office chart -- May 16-18.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are the final data for the top 10 movies at the May 16-18 box office, according to Exhibitor Relations Co.</p>
<p>    Film		   Three-day gross    Cumulative Gross</p>
<p>1. The Fifth Element	$11,410,863	 $ 34,213,330</p>
<p>2. Fathers' Day	     $ 6,108,652	 $ 17,207,686</p>
<p>3  Breakdown		  $ 5,947,444	 $ 31,239,767</p>
<p>4. Austin Powers...	 $ 5,844,089	 $ 27,507,435</p>
<p>5. Volcano		    $ 3,596,177	 $ 38,931,948</p>
<p>6. Liar Liar		  $ 3,202,550	 $160,615,430</p>
<p>7. Night Falls</p>
<p>    On Manhattan	    $ 2,933,255	 $  ----</p>
<p>8. Sprung		     $ 2,487,702,	$  3,002,040</p>
<p>9. Romy and Michele's</p>
<p>    High School Reunion   $ 2,240,691	 $ 22,295,923</p>
<p>10 Anaconda		   $ 2,220,707	 $ 56,005,753</p>
<p>NOTE: &quot;The Fifth Element&quot; was produced by Gaumont SA and released in the United States by Columbia Pictures, a unit of Sony Corp., which also released &quot;Anaconda.&quot;</p>
<p>&quot;Fathers' Day&quot; is released by Warner Bros., a unit of Time Warner Inc. Time Warner's New Line Cinema released &quot;Austin Powers: International Man of Mystery.&quot;</p>
<p>&quot;Breakdown&quot; and &quot;Night Falls on Manhattan&quot; are released by Paramount Pictures, a unit of Viacom Inc.</p>
<p>&quot;Volcano&quot; is released by 20th Century Fox, a unit of News Corp. &quot;Liar Liar&quot; is released by Universal Pictures, a unit of Seagram Co. Ltd.</p>
<p>&quot;Romy and Michele's High School Reunion&quot; is released by Walt Disney Co. &quot;Sprung&quot; is released by Trimark Pictures.</p>
</text>
